{
 "planTickAndStart": [
  [
   "modal",
   "Move copies · data",
   "<p class=\"ui-lead\">Move this volume's copies to disks with other tags, for example onto an NVMe drive. Each copy is rebuilt on a chosen disk before the old one is removed, so whatever uses the volume keeps running.</p><div id=\"cm_body\"><div class=\"empty\"><span class=\"spin2\"></span> reading where its copies are</div></div><div class=\"ui-actions\" >\n      <div class=\"ui-actions-start\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"closeModal()\" data-dialog-dismiss=\"true\">Cancel</button></div><div class=\"ui-actions-end\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn pri\" id=\"cm_go\" onclick=\"volumeCopyMoveStart()\" disabled >Move copies</button></div></div>",
   false,
   "operation-review"
  ],
  [
   "api",
   "/api/longhorn/copies/plan?volume=pvc-1&disk_tags=nvme&node_tags=",
   null
  ],
  [
   "applyRole"
  ],
  [
   "state",
   "planned",
   "<div class=\"ui-fields\"><div class=\"ui-field\">\n    <label for=\"field-c1\">Disk tags</label><div class=\"row wrap\" style=\"gap:6px\"><label class=\"check\"><input id=\"field-c1\" type=\"checkbox\" checked\n      onchange=\"volumeCopyMoveTag(&quot;disk&quot;,&quot;nvme&quot;,this.checked)\"> nvme</label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" \n      onchange=\"volumeCopyMoveTag(&quot;disk&quot;,&quot;ssd&quot;,this.checked)\"> ssd</label></div><div class=\"ui-help\">Copies go to disks carrying every tag ticked</div></div><div class=\"ui-field\">\n    <label for=\"field-c2\">Host tags</label><div class=\"row wrap\" style=\"gap:6px\"><label class=\"check\"><input id=\"field-c2\" type=\"checkbox\" \n      onchange=\"volumeCopyMoveTag(&quot;node&quot;,&quot;rack&lt;1&gt;&quot;,this.checked)\"> rack&lt;1&gt;</label></div></div></div><div class=\"ui-callout warn\" role=\"alert\">\n      <span class=\"ui-callout-icon\"><svg class=\"ui-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-alert\"/></svg></span>\n      <div><div class=\"ui-notice-line ui-notice-whole\"><b class=\"ui-notice-head\">Slow disk</b></div></div>\n    </div><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Its copies</h4></header>\n    <div class=\"ui-table-wrap\"><table class=\"ui-table stack\"><thead><tr><th class=\"\">Host</th><th class=\"\">Disk</th><th class=\"\">Tags</th><th class=\"\"></th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Host\">host-a</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Disk\"><span class=\"mono xs\">/var/a</span></td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Tags\">ssd</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"\"><span class=\"ui-chip info\">moves</span></td></tr><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Host\">host-b</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Disk\"><span class=\"mono xs\">/var/b</span></td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Tags\">nvme</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"\"><span class=\"ui-chip ok\">stays</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Disks it can go to</h4></header>\n    <div class=\"ui-table-wrap\"><table class=\"ui-table stack\"><thead><tr><th class=\"\">Host</th><th class=\"\">Disk</th><th class=\"\">Room</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Host\">host-c</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Disk\"><span class=\"mono xs\">/var/c</span></td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Room\">100 GiB</td></tr><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Host\">host-d</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Disk\"><span class=\"mono xs\">/var/d</span></td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Room\"><span class=\"ui-chip bad\">no room</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><dl class=\"ui-facts\"><div><dt>Size</dt><dd>10 GiB · 4 GiB written</dd></div><div><dt>State</dt><dd>in use on host-a</dd></div><div><dt>To move</dt><dd>1 of 2 copies, one at a time</dd></div></dl><details class=\"ui-more\" data-disclosure=\"What happens\">\n    <summary>What happens</summary><div class=\"ui-more-body\">The volume's disk and host tags are set, so Longhorn builds each new copy on a chosen disk. One extra copy is requested while each one is built, and the old copy is removed once the new one is complete, so the volume never has fewer complete copies than it needs. Its storage class name does not change, because a volume's class cannot change, only where its copies are stored. Copies that Longhorn rebuilds later follow the new tags. Stopping the job restores the old tags, and copies already moved stay where they are.</div></details>",
   false
  ],
