   "<div class=\"ui-fields\"><div class=\"ui-field\">\n    <label for=\"field-c1\">Disk tags</label><div class=\"row wrap\" style=\"gap:6px\"><label class=\"check\"><input id=\"field-c1\" type=\"checkbox\" \n      onchange=\"volumeCopyMoveTag(&quot;disk&quot;,&quot;nvme&quot;,this.checked)\"> nvme</label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" \n      onchange=\"volumeCopyMoveTag(&quot;disk&quot;,&quot;ssd&quot;,this.checked)\"> ssd</label></div><div class=\"ui-help\">Copies go to disks carrying every tag ticked</div></div><div class=\"ui-field\">\n    <label for=\"field-c2\">Host tags</label><div class=\"row wrap\" style=\"gap:6px\"><label class=\"check\"><input id=\"field-c2\" type=\"checkbox\" \n      onchange=\"volumeCopyMoveTag(&quot;node&quot;,&quot;rack&lt;1&gt;&quot;,this.checked)\"> rack&lt;1&gt;</label></div></div></div><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Its copies</h4></header>\n    <div class=\"ui-table-wrap\"><table class=\"ui-table stack\"><thead><tr><th class=\"\">Host</th><th class=\"\">Disk</th><th class=\"\">Tags</th><th class=\"\"></th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Host\">host-a</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Disk\"><span class=\"mono xs\">/var/a</span></td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Tags\">ssd</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"\"><span class=\"ui-chip info\">moves</span></td></tr><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Host\">host-b</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Disk\"><span class=\"mono xs\">/var/b</span></td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Tags\">nvme</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"\"></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Disks it can go to</h4></header>\n    <div class=\"ui-table-wrap\"><table class=\"ui-table stack\"><thead><tr><th class=\"\">Host</th><th class=\"\">Disk</th><th class=\"\">Room</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Host\">host-c</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Disk\"><span class=\"mono xs\">/var/c</span></td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Room\">100 GiB</td></tr><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Host\">host-d</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Disk\"><span class=\"mono xs\">/var/d</span></td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Room\"><span class=\"ui-chip bad\">no room</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><dl class=\"ui-facts\"><div><dt>Size</dt><dd>10 GiB · 4 GiB written</dd></div><div><dt>State</dt><dd>in use on host-a</dd></div><div><dt>To move</dt><dd>1 of 2 copies, one at a time</dd></div></dl><details class=\"ui-more\" data-disclosure=\"What happens\">\n    <summary>What happens</summary><div class=\"ui-more-body\">The volume's disk and host tags are set, so Longhorn builds each new copy on a chosen disk. One extra copy is requested while each one is built, and the old copy is removed once the new one is complete, so the volume never has fewer complete copies than it needs. Its storage class name does not change, because a volume's class cannot change, only where its copies are stored. Copies that Longhorn rebuilds later follow the new tags. Stopping the job restores the old tags, and copies already moved stay where they are.</div></details>",
